    "body": "Blocked. Two open issues block this work. No PR is open.\n\nCase 1 (Wire Contour from a DXF):\n- `import_dxf` imports the profile. `add_operation` adds the Wire Contour on it.\n- Generation refuses the operation: `this operation is checked against the stock 'Stock' and the chains of the DXF profile 'punch' (1 closed, 0 open) - there is no solid model; a toolpath from the chains of a DXF profile is not generated yet`.\n- #2022 tracks this gap. Its draft PRs #2978 and #2993 are by a contributor. They post DXF loops on the Agie only. They do not cover the Sodick ALC400G post, and they do not cover a profile with concave corners.\n- All other steps work on the Sodick ALC400G: `load_machine { builtin: \"Sodick ALC400G\" }`, `add_setup`, `set_setup_post { post: \"Sodick Wire EDM (Mark 21)\" }`, and `edit_machine` with a synthetic condition `C110`. The shipped machine file has no condition table, so the case must add one.\n\nCase 2 (taper refusal):\n- The catalog cannot compare a refusal yet. #2856 adds this. It is claimed and has no PR.\n\nHeld work: branch `mkinney:issue/2871-wire-edm-cases` at 9379e8e88. It has the DXF generator, the DXF and a draft `build.camscript`.\n\nNext step: when #2022 generates a Wire Contour on a DXF profile for the Sodick post, run `cargo xtask catalog --case edm/wire-contour` on that branch. Then add the README and the test module `catalog_edm_wire_contour` in `crates/app/tests/example_catalog.rs`. Add case 2 after #2856 merges.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
